sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Moulton, Goriely & Chirat (2015) & Chirat et al. (2013) hierarchical mollusc aperture spine folding and fractal frond serration — MorphoEval overall 87.5/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) remediated evaluation of `2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py` (weighted overall 87.5/100, DOWN from the 91.4/100 Pass 2 consensus). Both Pass 2 remediation items were closed with honestly labelled reduced models: a linearised Koiter/FvK mantle-margin surface with a varix growth window and oblique spiral-cord ridge forcing (`solve_koiter_shell_cord_spine_coupling`, L670-900; 17 free vs 16 cord-locked emergent spines, registration 1.00, locking tongue [1,2,5,9], de-registration at psi* = 35.0 deg with spine-ridge tilt), and an inverse-WKB specimen thickness gradient feeding a graded-rigidity comb (r = 0.991 to the local WKB wavelength) and an allometric instar series (beta* = 4/3) (`infer_specimen_thickness_gradient` / `solve_graded_thickness_comb` / `evaluate_ontogenetic_instar_series`, L1008-1190). The new emergent solvers, relaxed from noise, expose that the Pass 2 1-D comb count is pinned to round(L/lambda_1) by construction (L230-263), that the elastica, frond cascade and varix cycle are parametric/prescribed (L367-375, L411-417, L457-462), and that five reference values are the script's own outputs; these are the Pass 4 items. 13 self-test checks pass (74 s), 5 Lean theorems verify with 0 sorry, 5 dataset files are SHA-256-pinned, and the 3x3 figure, two GIFs and a standalone Pass 3 figure render. Overall 87.5/100 (faithfulness 86.4, reproducibility 90.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 9987db7d; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 86, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 84, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 90, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py at 9987db7d, image/png, 1194417 B, 2640×2400 px, artifact_sha256 1982f3f9822d1bbcf1b1f7746300e631c3f6c1877a192d1178f7c2019f4ea327 (sha256 1982f3f9822d1bbcf1b1f7746300e631c3f6c1877a192d1178f7c2019f4ea327), spec_fingerprint 7e0a58a2882e57518d985e4253c9b131677e4c5f4943a638d01e321b11b48932. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 7e0a58a2882e57518d985e4253c9b131677e4c5f4943a638d01e321b11b48932; artifact_sha256: 1982f3f9822d1bbcf1b1f7746300e631c3f6c1877a192d1178f7c2019f4ea327; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling/mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling_reference.json=c73e5d2ac5c13cd5..., datasets/mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling/murex_pecten_aperture_specimen.jpg=2f87d4ec30ebec6a..., datasets/mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling/paper_citations.bib=fc39398ba54f69e1..., datasets/mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling/pass3_koiter_cord_thickness_reference.json=63fdbb231492c336..., datasets/mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling/scout_manifest.json=53cb565add07b28d...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Chirat, Moulton & Goriely (2013): the mantle edge is an elastic strip growing against the calcified shell margin; excess growth gamma > gamma_c buckles it with wavelength lambda_1 ~ (E h_1^3 / 3 K_s)^(1/4) set by the mantle thickness and the foundation stiffness, giving comb spines along the siphonal canal of Murex pecten and varix spines in muricids | Moulton, Goriely & Chirat (2015): further growth folds each spine into a Kirchhoff elastica loop that self-contacts into a hollow tube, and thinner secondary/tertiary mantle generations produce the fractal frond cascade k_{i+1}/k_i = (h_i/h_{i+1})^(3/4) of Chicoreus ramosus | Rudraraju et al. (2019): the full problem is a finite-strain morphoelastic shell with surface and volume growth, solved by finite elements | Koiter (1966) and Manor, Hagberg & Meron (2008): the thin-shell energy used for the reduced surface model, and wave-number locking of a pattern-forming system to a spatially periodic forcing (Arnold tongues); reconstructed_in_script: Hierarchical wavenumber law k_i^* = (3 K_s / (E h_i^3))^(1/4); 1-D unilateral fourth-order comb energy minimised by L-BFGS-B at the rounded mode q_mode = 2 pi round(L/lambda_1)/L; parametric omega-loop spine profile with a linear neck-gap law; prescribed 3-stage frond cosines; prescribed 120 deg varix bursts; 10-species cross-taxa table; DoG specimen segmentation (Pass 2) | Pass 3: reduced linearised Koiter/FvK surface w(s,t) on a 192x96 bi-periodic torus (L_s = 67.2 mm, L_t = 24 mm, D = 1, K_0 = (k_1^*)^4) with varix growth window P(t), additive cord ridge forcing, semi-implicit gradient flow + L-BFGS-B relaxation from noise, emergent spine count / cord-intersection registration / ridge tilt; locking-tongue and obliquity sweeps; inverse-WKB h(u) from the specimen spacing profile; graded-rigidity 1-D comb with uniform control; allometric instar series with Brent root beta*; transfer_boundary: The Koiter surface is linearised (no finite membrane strain, flat reference torus, nondimensional D = 1 with outputs labelled mm) and the planar elastica cross-section is not coupled to it; both are separate modules, so the Pass 2 item 1 (3D finite-strain Koiter FE coupling) is addressed only in reduced form | h(s) is inferred from a Murex pecten photograph via inverse WKB (R^2 = 0.29, floor 0.35), not measured by micro-CT, and the species is not the Chicoreus ramosus the Pass 2 item asked for; no Chicoreus specimen is vendored | The 1-D comb spine count 16, the 120 deg varix spacing, the Chicoreus k_2/k_1 = 3.80, the neck-gap delta -3.1059 mm, the specimen CV 0.2092 reference, beta* = 4/3 and the rigid-spine 22.8 deg are prescribed or self-referential and must not be read as validations; does_not_claim: A finite-strain shell FE solution, a numerically integrated Kirchhoff-Clebsch elastica, emergent fractal frond serrations, emergent varix periodicity, measured mantle thickness data for any species, or sourced empirical k_2/k_1 and spine counts for the 10 muricid species." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py:1008-1044 and 585 — the inverse-WKB thickness profile is inferred from a Murex pecten photograph (two-harmonic fit R^2 = 0.29, arbitrary 0.35 floor at L1031) and the first segmented spacing (find_peaks distance 26 px) is plausibly spurious. Vendor measured mantle-edge h(s) cross-sections (micro-CT or histology) for *Chicoreus ramosus* across at least two instars with the empirical allometric exponent beta, and exclude or justify the first spacing.",
            "remediation needed: 2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py:163, 213, 677 — two foundation stiffnesses for the same law (K_s = 0.48 for the frond cascade, K_s_eff = 1.98 for comb/Koiter/graded); `--K-s` (L1985) reaches only the frond synthesiser (L1263). Unify on one sourced K_s (or document the effective-vs-material distinction) and thread `--K-s` and `--E` through every solver including the elastica and varix modules; fix the stale \"8-check\" help text (L1981).",
            "remediation needed: 2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py:1826, 1866, 1773, 1236 — reference values that equal the script's own output or an analytic identity (neck-gap delta -3.1059; specimen CV 0.2092; beta* = 4/3; rigid psi* 22.78 deg). Replace each with an external anchor (e.g. literature spine-spacing CV for Murex pecten, measured neck gaps from Moulton 2015 Fig. 6) or mark `reference_value: null` with `derived_from: model`.",
            "remediation needed: 2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py:1874-1976 — self-test wall time ~65-75 s because the locking and obliquity sweeps run at full resolution; add a reduced-resolution fast path (n_s = 96, n_t = 48 as at L1941) for the sweeps under `--self-test` and keep the full sweeps behind a flag.",
            "remediation needed: 2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py:230-263 — `solve_murex_siphonal_comb` builds the foundation from the rounded mode q_mode = 2 pi round(L/lambda_1)/L (k_sub = q_mode^4, L256) and seeds the 16-mode (L263), so the \"L-BFGS-B relaxed spine count 16.0 vs 16.0\" measurement (L1812-1820) is prescribed. Replace with the Koiter-style noise initialisation on K_0 = (k_1^*)^4 (as at L670-900) so the count is emergent (theory 16.47), and relabel the measurement; also make `EI_eff`, `P_load`, `kappa_3` dimensional or drop the `_mm` suffixes (L255-260).",
            "remediation needed: 2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py:335-386 and 43-44 — `solve_kirchhoff_elastica_spine_loop` does not integrate the Kirchhoff-Clebsch ODE stated in the header; it draws a parametric omega loop (cos^1.8 profile, L375) with a linear neck gap (L364) and an uncited height law 4.8 sqrt(gamma - gamma_c) (L368, reused at L747). Integrate the elastica with unilateral self-contact (shooting or collocation) and couple its cross-section to the Koiter surface height scale, closing the residual of Pass 2 item 1.",
            "remediation needed: 2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py:411-417 and 457-462 — the Chicoreus frond stages are hand-drawn cosines and the varix cycle prescribes 120 deg Gaussian bursts, so the k_2/k_1 = 3.80 (L1806; h_2 = 0.0708 chosen at L182/L391 to hit it) and the 120.0 deg (L1836) measurements are circular. Derive the secondary serrations by solving the comb energy on the primary frond with h_2, and let varix spacing emerge from a growth-rate / rest-period dynamic (Lean Law 3) instead of a prescribed gamma(phi).",
            "remediation needed: 2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py:497-556 with datasets/mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling/mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling_reference.json:114-150 — `k2_over_k1_obs`, `n_primary_spines_obs`, h_1 and h_2 per species have no measurement source and match the predictions to rounding (r = 1.0000 / 0.9987). Source each row to a published figure/table or relabel the table as model-generated and drop the two cross-taxa correlations from `measure_morphoeval()`.",
            "remediation needed: 2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py:670-900 — the Koiter surface is linearised on a flat bi-periodic torus with D = 1 (nondimensional) and periodic t with subcritical margins; the free count 17 is quantised by the domain and shifted by onset excess (q_max = sqrt(P/2)); `converged` falls back to a gradient-norm test at maxiter (L817); the height-modulation metric is uninformative for locked patterns. Add reference-surface curvature and finite membrane strain (or a true FE shell per Rudraraju 2019), report D in N mm, test domain-size independence of the free count, and remove or replace the hmod metric." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.875"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (Pass 3 remediated assessment, Phase B audit agent)" ;
        dct:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

